/// Wire goldens for the JS-number codec arm: values, and the bytes a real
/// 64-bit `setInt64` produces for them.
///
/// GENERATED by `bazel run //runtime/dart:js_arm_web_test -- --goldens`.
/// Do not hand-edit: `js_numbers_test` re-derives every row from `setInt64`
/// on the VM, so an edited byte fails there rather than silently weakening
/// the browser half that consumes it.
///
/// The two halves exist because neither backend can do the job alone: dart2js
/// has no `setInt64` to compare against, and the VM cannot reproduce the arm's
/// one double-specific hazard — reconstructing 2^53 + 1 rounds it down to
/// 2^53, so a guard on the reconstructed value passes there and fails here.
library;

